{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1462805-city-of-mist-conversion-for-tc-aberrant","id":1462805,"title":"City of Mist Conversion for TC: Aberrant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-05T09:28:10-07:00","id":1462805,"title":"City of Mist Conversion for TC: Aberrant","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I love the setting of Aberrant (both old and new) and I also love the Storypath system. However, my friends and I have not been able to kick how cool we find the City of Mist version of Powered by the Apocalypse. So, I have taken on a side-project to convert the City of Mist system for the TC: Aberrant setting.<br /> <br /> I am posting here to share the work I get done on the project, but to also invite others to provide their suggestions and ideas. I am still in early days, but I am excited about figuring this out. I am leaning into an understanding of the Aberrant setting that pulls from the old materials and the new materials. I always enjoyed the capecore and horror elements of the original materials, but think the new setting is a bit tidier in its structure. I believe the City of Mist mechanics really support both players and MC\u2019s in navigating the tension (and at times horror) between Baseline life and Nova life. I am hoping the mechanical adaptations and changes I make can highlight that particular dynamism I find so enjoyable about the Aberrant setting.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","user":"lladas","date":". 10-06-2021, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T05:14:49-07:00","id":1462884,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Terminology Changes</span></span></b></span></b></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Here are some changes to the terminology of City of Mist that first came to mind. I am still in the process of changing over everything so I will have edits to language on this post.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Rifts are called Novas</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Logos </i>themes are called <i>Baseline</i>. These themes represent the normal parts of <i>Novas </i>lives</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Replace <i>Mythos </i>themes with <i>Quantum </i>themes. These themes represent the variety of quantum abilities found among <i>Novas</i>.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u200bChange the <i>Mystery </i>on <i>Quantum </i>Theme Cards to <i>Eruption </i>to represent either what caused the <i>Nova </i>power to awaken or what can cause it to be used uncontrollably or inappropriately (e.g., to resolve a mundane issue, assert your godhood). These <i>Eruption </i>should be declarations or descriptions, not questions.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Change <i>Fade </i>to <i>Grounding </i>to represent the character choosing to push down the urge to use their power or forcing it to go Dormant.\u200b</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Here are the list of <i>Quantum </i>themes I came up with and some examples for each. </span></spa